    "body": "**Stacked on #482** (#339 slice 4, fixture UX), which is on #476. Slice 6 of #339 per the triage on the issue: a fixture library.\n\n## What changed\n**The library file.** One `fixtures.camfixtures` in the user fixtures folder: `CAMCRAFT_FIXTURES` (an absolute path), otherwise `<data dir>/camcraft/fixtures`, beside the machines folder.\n- Versioned envelope: `{format: \"camcraft-fixtures\", version: 1, units: \"mm\", fixtures: [{name, note?, datum: {origin, rot}, facets}]}`. Save → load → save is byte-stable.\n- **Refused by name, whole file:** bad JSON; wrong format, version or units; a missing name, datum or facets; a duplicate name; an empty mesh; a malformed facet; a rotation that isn't one; over 2M facets; the reserved `Machine/Table` name.\n- A missing file reads as an empty library. A corrupt one is reported in the dialog, never shown as empty, and never overwritten.\n- The atomic write mirrors #383's machine store. It's a short copy, to be folded into one helper once both land; see the decisions file.\n\n**The datum.**\n- An entry's facets are the fixture's own model-frame mesh, and its datum is a frame in that mesh.\n- On insert, the model's pose is `P ∘ D⁻¹`, so the datum lands on the pick.\n- The default datum is the model origin, so a fixture saved and re-inserted at its old pose stands exactly where it was. The other choice is \"Bottom centre\".\n\n**Duplicate names:**\n- In the library, saving an existing name asks \"Replace …?\". There is no silent rename.\n- In the document, an inserted name that's taken lands as \"Vise (2)\", \"Vise (3)\" and so on.\n\n**`InsertFixture`, one undo unit.** It spawns the model with the entry's facets, sets its pose, and tags it to the Fixtures node's setup. It refuses by name a setup that no longer exists, a non-finite or non-rotation pick, or a bad entry. There is no new project key: inserted fixtures are ordinary tagged models.\n\n**Save and delete edit the library file.** They are save actions with confirmation, not undo entries, like machine files (#383).\n\n**UI.** The setup's Fixtures node menu gains **Save fixture to library…** and **Insert from library…**, each a modal dialog.\n- **Save:** the setup's fixtures as checkboxes, the datum choice, and a note.\n- **Insert:** the entry list, X/Y/Z in display units, and roll/pitch/yaw. Buttons are Insert, **Delete from library…** (with confirmation) and Close.\n- Picking the datum in the viewport is a follow-up.\n\nAll assets are user-made; no vendor libraries.\n\n`docs/decisions/339-fixture-library.md`\n\n## How tested\n- App `fixture_library` (6 tests):\n  - envelope round-trip, and refusals by name;\n  - the folder resolver;\n  - save, replace and delete file edits;\n  - the datum placement maths;\n  - insert with undo, redo and the project round-trip.\n- UI `egui_app::fixture_library_tests` (4 tests, driven through the real dialog):\n  - the menu rows;\n  - save, then the replace confirmation;\n  - Insert queues one undoable command, and delete happens only after confirmation;\n  - a corrupt library is named in the dialog.\n- Regressions green: app `fixture_ux` 8, `fixtures` 14, `commands_undo` 32, `fixture_mesh` 3; ui lib 352, ui `tests/fixtures` 7, `tests/models` 4. One #482 test's menu-label list now includes the two new rows.\n- Known failures: the headless-GPU test, and the release-lane `tool_editor_snapshot`.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft until the contributor's GUI check)\nA hands-on check. The test kit is prepared and sandboxed with `CAMCRAFT_FIXTURES`.\n\nChangelog: A fixture library: save fixtures (mesh + placement datum) to a versioned library file and insert them into a setup at a datum in one undoable step (#339)\n\nRefs #339\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
